  "verbalization": "Latifoloside A is proposed to interact with the CD276 antigen through a multi-step mechanism involving cyclin-dependent kinase 2/cyclin E. The evidence suggests that Latifoloside A targets cyclin-dependent kinase 2/cyclin E, which in turn is a target of another compound, 2-[7-[(1S)-1-(4-Hydroxyphenyl)Ethyl]-4-Methoxy-1H-Indol-3-Yl]Acetonitrile, which ultimately binds to the CD276 antigen. This indicates a potential pathway where Latifoloside A may exert its effect by modulating the activity of cyclin-dependent kinase 2/cyclin E, thereby influencing the CD276 antigen. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though further validation is needed to confirm the specific mode of action and the biological relevance of the observed interactions. The mechanism appears to involve a cascade of targets, with the CD276 antigen being the final endpoint in this chain.",
